{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>He and Hoshea bin Nun.</b> Meaning, he was standing with him; but the speech — only Moshe spoke, as the verse says ״וַיְדַבֵּר״. And so HaShem said, ״וְלַמְּדָהּ אֶת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל שִׂימָהּ בְּפִיהֶם״ — in singular language, to Moshe. And the verse's saying ״וְהוֹשֵׁעַ״ and not ״וִיהוֹשֻׁעַ״ as Moshe called him — this is because the addition of the yud is for honor and greatness, as alluded to in the verse (Numbers 13:16) ״וַיִּקְרָא מֹשֶׁה לְהוֹשֵׁעַ״ etc.; and when the verse equated them and said ״הוּא וְהוֹשֵׁעַ בִּן נוּן״, it removed the yud, in the manner of the verse (Isaiah 10:15) ״הֲיִתְפָּאֵר הַגַּרְזֶן״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:46.988928020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}